        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Tiwanaku – Moon Valley – La Paz"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "d4624ad8eb9b955f9fb8bde9c1909e42687a1866a3db6fab16886f6827b9360b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-worker-d585b2821829f1fdbfcb5695",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "After breakfast, we head to the Tiwanaku archaeological complex.\n\nIt lies about 70 km from La Paz at an elevation of around 4,000 m. The complex is a UNESCO World Heritage Site.\n\nYou will visit the Kalasasaya Temple, the Akapana Pyramid, the ceramics museum, the Gateway of the Sun and the Ponce Monolith.\n\nAfter the visit, we return to La Paz. Lunch is at your own expense.\n\nIn the afternoon, we drive to Valle de la Luna (Moon Valley), about 10 km from the city. Erosion has shaped the landscape into unusual rock formations and narrow ridges.\n\nFrom Moon Valley, we return to the city and take a cable car for a view of La Paz from above.\n\nNext, we visit the historic centre, the Witches' Market, San Francisco Church, Plaza Murillo and the Presidential Palace.\n\nThe tour ends at the Killi Killi viewpoint.\n\nReturn to your hotel."
    },
